<title>USA: Texaco, Shell, Saudi Aramco talk unit merger - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Texaco, Shell, Saudi Aramco talk unit merger - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. oil giants Texaco Inc, Shell Oil Co and a Saudi Arabian company are negotiating the merger of their U.S. refining and marketing businesses in a deal that would pool assets valued at more than $10 billion, the Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the merger would combine the &quot;downstream forces&quot; of Texaco, Shell, the U.S. unit of Royal Dutch/Shell Group and Star Enterprise, a joint venture between Texaco and Saudi Aramco, the state oil company of Saudi Arabia.</p>
</text>
